course: dictionary
lesson: 13505
title: Imminent: about to happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Imminent is an adjective, a describing word. It means about to happen very soon, and it is often used for something bad or dangerous. «The sky went black and the thunder grew louder: a storm was imminent.» The clouds and thunder are the clues. A storm that is coming in a few minutes is imminent.
explain: Newspapers, weather reports and safety signs use imminent to give a warning. «Warning: flood imminent. Move to higher ground.» The sign does not say the flood happened. It says the flood is so close that you must act now.
explain: In stories, imminent builds tension, the feeling of something about to go wrong. «The door creaked. Danger was imminent.» To check your meaning, swap in "about to happen very soon". If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Imminent means about to happen very soon.
fact: Imminent is often used for bad or dangerous things, such as a storm or a flood.
fact: Common phrases are imminent danger, imminent arrival and an imminent storm.
fact: Imminent is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «imminent danger».
exercise: «Ravi saw black clouds and heard thunder. A storm is imminent.» What does imminent mean? | Gone for ever | *About to happen very soon | Happy and calm | Very small and far away
exercise: Which phrase warns you of something bad that is about to happen? | A long, quiet sleep | A bright summer day | *Imminent danger | A happy birthday song
exercise: «The rocket's launch is imminent: the countdown has reached five.» Why does the countdown help you guess the meaning? | It shows the rocket is very big | It shows nobody will launch anything | It shows the launch was yesterday | *It shows the launch will happen very soon
test: «The bus arrival is imminent, so grab your bag now.» What is the closest meaning of imminent? | Long ago | Far away in the future | *Very soon | Hidden under the sea
test: Which sentence uses imminent correctly? | Our old toys are imminent, they were made years ago | *The rain is imminent, so take an umbrella | Imminent is a kind of cake we eat at tea | The imminent sun rose at noon
exam: A sign reads «Flood imminent». What should you do? | Ask for a sweet to calm down | Go for a swim in the river | Ignore it, because floods are rare | *Move to higher ground quickly
